<section class="page-header card">
  <p class="eyebrow">Design system</p>
  <h2>Website style guide</h2>
  <p class="lede">Use this page to keep new pages and components consistent. Lean on the existing palette, typography, spacing tokens, and cards so everything feels like DUE even as layouts grow.</p>
</section>

<section class="card-grid">
  <article class="card panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Approach</p>
    <h3 class="card-title">Tone and hierarchy</h3>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li>Lead with concise headlines and a short lede; reserve long-form text for essays.</li>
      <li>Use cards to group related ideas and to provide consistent padding, borders, and shadows.</li>
      <li>Favor inline links over buttons except for high-intent actions like comments.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
  <article class="card panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Accessibility</p>
    <h3 class="card-title">Readable defaults</h3>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li>Keep the body copy at 16px with the UI font stack and reserve headings for the essay font.</li>
      <li>Use the <code>.skip-link</code> and breadcrumb output baked into the base layout; avoid removing them.</li>
      <li>Links should remain high-contrast and underlined on hover; avoid custom focus outlines.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
  <article class="card panel">
    <p class="eyebrow">Spacing</p>
    <h3 class="card-title">Scale and shells</h3>
    <ul class="muted">
      <li>Default spacing tokens come from <code>--space-2xs</code> through <code>--space-2xl</code>; stick to them for gaps and padding.</li>
      <li>Pages sit in a <code>.page-shell</code> with generous inline padding; avoid edge-to-edge layouts.</li>
      <li>Card padding is controlled by <code>--space-card-padding-block</code> and <code>--space-card-padding-inline</code> so grids stay aligned.</li>
    </ul>
  </article>
</section>

