<section class="card">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Components</p>
    <h3>Reusable building blocks</h3>
    <p class="muted">Start with the default card, then add small variations for context instead of crafting one-off modules.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card-grid">
    <article class="card panel">
      <h4 class="card-title">Cards and panels</h4>
      <p class="muted">Use <code>.card</code> for most sections; apply <code>.panel</code> for lighter, dashed outlines on secondary content. <code>.card-grid</code> and <code>.grid-two</code> keep responsive columns even.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card panel">
      <h4 class="card-title">Badges and pills</h4>
      <p class="muted">Use <code>.length-chip</code> and <code>.legend-badge</code> for word-count cues. Length chips follow the standard bands: Tiny (100–500 words, purple square), Minute (500–1000 words, warm orange triangle), and Short (1000–1500 words, teal circle). Use <code>.badge--tone-*</code> for status messaging and <code>.accent-pill</code> for inline notes.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="card panel">
      <h4 class="card-title">Heroes and banners</h4>
      <p class="muted">The <code>.hero.spotlight</code> layout provides a soft gradient frame, while <code>.hero__panel</code> and <code>.hero__visual</code> boxes handle supporting copy and imagery.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
