<section class="card">
  <div class="section-heading">
    <p class="eyebrow">Interaction</p>
    <h3>Links, forms, and motion</h3>
    <p class="muted">Keep interactions predictable and avoid bespoke hover states so the brand remains calm and deliberate.</p>
  </div>
  <ul class="muted">
    <li>Default links inherit the accent color and gain an underline on hover; avoid replacing them with buttons unless the action is primary (e.g., commenting).</li>
    <li>Reuse the inline comment metadata pattern (<code>.comment__eyebrow</code>, <code>.comment__meta</code>, and <code>.comment</code> stack) for any reader-submitted blocks.</li>
    <li>Respect form defaults: use <code>label</code> elements, leave focus outlines intact, and keep inputs in stacked layouts with <code>--space-sm</code> gaps.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
